### C. Unfamiliar application submission

This is a critical evaluator scenario.

The assignment allows submission by application name OR website.

Test all cases:

1. Known provider name only.
2. Known provider URL only.
3. Unfamiliar provider name only.
4. Unfamiliar provider URL only.
5. Name and URL together.
6. Empty name and URL.
7. Invalid URL.
8. URL with an unsupported protocol.
9. URL with credentials embedded.
10. URL containing suspicious or unsafe destinations.
11. App name containing unusual characters.
12. Duplicate investigation.
13. Existing provider name with an incorrect URL.
14. Name inferred from URL.
15. User correction of inferred name.

Expected behavior:

- Name-only submissions must be accepted as input.
- Known provider names should resolve only through verified registry entries.
- Unfamiliar names must not trigger fabricated documentation URLs.
- If a reliable official documentation URL cannot be found, the user must receive a clear, actionable next step.
